<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saadi dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saadian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Saadi dynasty was a family of Arab sharifs who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> from the sixteenth to the mid-seventeenth century. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-malik-i-saadi-sultan">Sultan Abd al-Malik</a> its forces defeated a Portuguese invasion at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alcacer-quibir">Battle of Alcácer Quibir</a> in 1578, in which King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebastian-of-portugal">Sebastian of Portugal</a> was killed. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> profile treats the defeat as a disaster that contributed to the Portuguese succession crisis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saadi-dynasty.jpg" alt="Saadi dynasty" width="320" height="278" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: R Prazeres · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saadiens_-_Carte_fin_XVIe_si%C3%A8cle_(revised).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
